and it was a deadly weekend in las vegas  after several pedestrians were killed  nhp  sending out a message to all of the  community about safety as we roll into  saint patrick's day  christian cazares live in studio with  more on these cases  and the nhp game plan that's right brian  well the nhp tells me yesterday was  quote a grim and busy day  in las vegas incidents that could have  all been prevented now take a look here  on your screen this was the scene near  lake mead and lambs  on sunday evening around 9. a pedestrian  was struck by a vehicle as  it was traveling west on lake mead the  victim was taken to the hospital and did  not survive  a few hours before on sunday another  pedestrian was struck  investigators say a white ford pickup  killed the person on sahara and 6th  street  but it was this scene on sunday morning  near prim that has the nevada highway  patrol  very concerned we had a sedan that was  traveling  southbound on i-15 near gene  when one of the occupants or the vehicle  pulled over to the right shoulder and  one of the occupants  exited the vehicle and entered the  northbound travel lane  in order to retrieve some property at  which time  they were struck well if you have an  emergency while driving you should  always pull off to the shoulder as far  as possible  and according to the nhp remain in your  vehicle it's illegal for someone  to be on the highway in the state of  nevada because of how dangerous it can  be  now none of the victims have been  identified nhp also says they will be in  full force for st  patrick's day on wednesday they will be  working with metro police and will be  looking for any impaired drivers  they say the best decision you can make  is to plan ahead and of course  don't drink and drive christian casadas  8 news now
 

